from lib import *
U='b2-boliviaoriente'
chall('bolivia-lowlands',{
f'{U}-01':C('The Missions Were Founded by Jesuits','You are Carlos. You and Meg are watching a documentary about the Chiquitos missions, and she asks who founded them.','Tell Meg who founded the missions and when the first one was founded.',['Say who founded the missions','Say the year of the first one'],'Las misiones fueron fundadas por jesuitas, y la primera fue fundada en 1691.','The missions were founded by Jesuits, and the first one was founded in 1691.','I can say what was founded, expelled and restored with *ser* + past participle.'),
f'{U}-02':C('A Big City, but a Small Past','You are Meg. You and Carlos are reading an article about Santa Cruz, and he asks if it was always a big city.','Tell Carlos that it is large today but was small before.',['Say that it is the largest city','Contrast it with its past'],'Santa Cruz es hoy la ciudad más poblada de Bolivia; sin embargo, durante siglos fue una población pequeña.','Santa Cruz is today the most populous city in Bolivia; however, for centuries it was a small town.','I can contrast two ideas about Santa Cruz with *sin embargo*, *no obstante* and *aunque*.'),
f'{U}-03':C('Apparently, Still Without Approval','You are Carlos. You and Meg are preparing a talk about lithium, and she asks about the contracts of 2024.','Tell Meg, with a hedge, what the situation of the contracts is in 2026.',['Soften your claim','Say that Congress has not approved them'],'Según parece, los contratos de 2024 todavía no tienen la aprobación del Congreso.','Apparently, the contracts of 2024 still do not have the approval of Congress.','I can soften a claim about lithium with *parece que*, *según parece* and *podría decirse que*.'),
f'{U}-04':C('If They Had Had More Water','You are Meg. You and Carlos are visiting a museum exhibition about the Chaco War, and he asks what made the war so hard.','Tell Carlos what would have helped the soldiers.',['Start with a condition about the past','Say that they would have suffered less'],'Si los soldados hubieran tenido más agua, habrían sufrido menos.','If the soldiers had had more water, they would have suffered less.','I can talk about a past that did not happen with *si* + *hubiera* + participle and *habría* + participle.'),
f'{U}-05':C('The Dancers Who Wear Masks','You are Carlos. You and Meg are watching a video of the Oruro carnival, and she asks who the dancers in masks are.','Tell Meg who the dancers with masks are playing.',['Describe the dancers','Say who they represent'],'Los bailarines que llevan máscaras de diablos participan en la diablada.','The dancers who wear devil masks take part in the diablada.','I can describe the dances and the people of the Oruro carnival with *que*, *quien* and *donde*.'),
f'{U}-consolidation':C('The Lowlands in Review','You are Meg. You and Carlos are preparing a short talk about the Bolivian lowlands, and he asks when the missions were declared World Heritage Sites.','Tell Carlos when UNESCO declared the missions a World Heritage Site.',['Say what was declared','Say the year'],'Las seis misiones fueron declaradas Patrimonio de la Humanidad en 1990.','The six missions were declared World Heritage Sites in 1990.','I can review what I learned about the Chiquitos missions, Santa Cruz, Uyuni, the Chaco War and the Oruro carnival.')})
